      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 1994,
      "text": "An array contains integers in locations $A [ 0 ], A [ 1 ], \\dotsc A [ n - 1 ]$. It is required to shift the elements of the array cyclically to the left by places, where $1 \\overset { \\cdot } { \\leq } K \\leq n \\overset { \\cdot } { - } 1$. An incomplete algorithm for doing this in linear time, without using another array is given below. Complete the algorithm by filling in the blanks. Assume all variables are suitably declared.",
      "options": [],
      "code_blocks": [
        {
          "lang": "txt",
          "code": "min:=n;\ni=0;\nwhile ______ do\nbegin\n    temp:=A[i];\n    j:=i;\n    while ______ do\n    begin\n        A[j]:=________;\n        j:=(j+K) mod n;\n        if j<min then\n            min:=j;\n        end;\n        A[(n+i-K) mod n]:=________;\n        i:=________;\n    end;"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
        "source_file": "filter1_volume2.pdf",
