      "kind": "pyq",
      "type": "mcq",
      "marks": 2,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "year": 2016,
      "text": "The following function computes $X ^ { Y }$ for positive integers and. Which one of the following conditions is TRUE before every iteration of the loop?",
      "options": [
        "XY = ab",
        "(res \\* a)Y = (res \\* X)b",
        "XY = res \\* ab",
        "XY = (res \\* a)b"
      ],
      "answer": [
        2
      ],
      "code_blocks": [
        {
          "lang": "lisp",
          "code": "int exp (int X, int Y) {\n    int res =1, a = X, b = Y;\n\n    while (b != 0) {\n        if (b % 2 == 0) {a = a * a; b = b/2; }\n        else        {res = res * a; b = b - 1; }\n    }\n    return res;\n}"
        }
      ],
      "origin": {
